@startuml 05-sequence-join-group
' SpendSnap — Joining a shared group by invite code, and how the
' server-side rules constrain the mutation to a self-join.

title SpendSnap — Sequence: Join a Shared Group by Invite Code

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2563EB
  ActorBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  BoxBorderColor #CBD5E1
  BoxBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "Joiner (Bob)" as U
box "Client" #F8FAFC
  participant "GroupScreen" as SCR
  participant "GroupCard" as CARD
  participant "services/firebase.js" as SVC
end box
box "Server tier — Firebase" #FFFBEB
  participant "Security Rules" as RULES
  database "Cloud Firestore" as FS
end box

U -> SCR : paste invite code (= groupId), tap Join
activate SCR
SCR -> SVC : joinGroup(uid, groupId)
activate SVC

SVC -> SVC : trim code; reject if empty
SVC -> RULES : setDoc(groups/{groupId},\n{members: {bob: true},\n memberEmails: {bob: "bob@…"}},\n {merge: true})
activate RULES

RULES -> FS : read existing group document
FS --> RULES : resource.data

RULES -> RULES : ownerId unchanged?\nchanged keys ⊆ {members, memberEmails}?

alt valid self-join
  RULES -> RULES : isSelfJoin(members, memberEmails)\n• group is not archived\n• members.diff().affectedKeys().hasOnly([bob])\n• incoming.members[bob] == true\n• bob ∉ existing.members\n• memberEmails.diff().affectedKeys().hasOnly([bob])\n• incoming.memberEmails[bob] is string
  RULES --> SVC : allow
else group has been archived by its owner
  RULES --> SVC : **PERMISSION_DENIED**
else tries to add or remove someone else,\nrelabel another member's email,\nrename, or change ownerId
  RULES --> SVC : **PERMISSION_DENIED**
end
deactivate RULES

note right of RULES
  `list` on groups is denied — a group can only be
  reached by a **known id**, never discovered.
  A typo'd code fails validation rather than
  silently creating a bogus group.
end note

note over RULES, FS
  There is no blanket "any member may update" branch.
  Every allowed update is one narrow, self-scoped case:
  **self-join** · **self-leave** · **own email label** ·
  **owner rename** (only `name`) · **owner archive**
  (only `archived` + `archivedAt`).
end note

SVC -> FS : setDoc(users/bob/settings/groups,\n{ids: arrayUnion(groupId)}, merge)
FS --> SVC : ok
SVC --> SCR : groupId
deactivate SVC

== Everything below happens live, without a refresh ==
FS -->> SCR : onSnapshot(settings/groups) → groupIds now includes groupId
SCR -> CARD : render GroupCard(groupId)
activate CARD
CARD -> SVC : subscribeToGroup(groupId)
CARD -> SVC : subscribeToGroupExpenses(groupId)
SVC -> FS : onSnapshot(collectionGroup("expenses")\nwhere groupIds array-contains groupId\norderBy date desc)
FS --> CARD : group doc + members + group expenses
CARD -> SVC : ensureMemberEmail(groupId, uid, email)\n<size:10>backfill for pre-email groups</size>
CARD -> U : invite code, members by email,\nper-member pie chart, running total
deactivate CARD
deactivate SCR

note over CARD
  **Starts at 0 by design.** An expense carries this
  groupId only when its author ticks the group while
  logging it, so joining never exposes Bob's history —
  past or personal-only spending stays private.
end note

@enduml
